WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.512
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:10.782 --> 00:13.576
Hello, everyone. I'm Kim Seong-bae, your commentator

3
00:13.660 --> 00:17.497
for the 2014 SNT National Track and Field Competition.`

4
00:17.997 --> 00:21.668
And now, it's finally time for the middle school girls' 200-meter final,

5
00:21.751 --> 00:23.920
where eight athletes are lining up to start.

6
00:24.003 --> 00:27.298
In lane eight, we have Byeon Ji-yoon from Cheolma Girls' Middle School.

7
00:27.382 --> 00:29.425
She's the favorite to win coming into the race.

8
00:29.509 --> 00:32.512
Absolutely. In terms of skill, no one can beat her off the blocks

9
00:32.595 --> 00:33.596
or match her drive phase.

10
00:33.680 --> 00:35.765
However, because of her poor performance in the semis,

11
00:35.849 --> 00:37.267
she'll be starting from lane eight.

12
00:37.350 --> 00:39.102
I've heard from several sources

13
00:39.185 --> 00:41.229
that Byeon Ji-yoon has a peculiar jinx.

14
00:41.312 --> 00:45.024
Whenever she's in lane eight, her record seems to fall apart.

15
00:45.108 --> 00:48.444
Here's hoping that's not the case today.

16
00:48.528 --> 00:51.948
What kind of time will she show us in the final? We're about to find out.

17
00:53.116 --> 00:55.577
That sound of the pistol means we're off!

18
00:55.660 --> 00:58.788
Ji-yoon is starting strong with an early burst of speed.

19
00:58.872 --> 01:02.417
But the question remains, can she finish strong? It's not over till it's over.

20
01:04.043 --> 01:06.754
What's the point of starting strong if you always fall behind?

21
01:06.838 --> 01:08.214
- Come on! - Come on, go!

22
01:09.340 --> 01:10.925
Pick it up! Pick it up!

23
01:11.634 --> 01:14.512
Don't think about anything else. Don't let anyone pass you.

24
01:14.596 --> 01:17.056
If you don't win this time, it's over. What if I can't?

25
01:17.140 --> 01:19.058
Just look ahead and run. Are they right behind me?

26
01:19.142 --> 01:20.852
No such thing as a jinx. Just focus.

27
01:20.935 --> 01:23.271
Focus until the finish line. You have to win.

28
01:23.354 --> 01:25.064
You can't make any mistakes. You can do this.

29
01:25.148 --> 01:26.024
Wait.

30
01:27.066 --> 01:28.610
Something feels off.

31
01:48.963 --> 01:49.923
Get up!

32
01:50.506 --> 01:51.507
Get up!

33
01:52.133 --> 01:53.468
I said, get up!

34
02:09.609 --> 02:11.736
I didn't want to work there anyway.

35
02:11.819 --> 02:13.947
UNFORTUNATELY, YOU HAVE NOT BEEN SELECTED FOR THE JOB

36
03:09.919 --> 03:12.839
DEAD-END JOB

37
03:14.173 --> 03:17.051
MIDNIGHT FANTASY CINEMA

38
03:18.094 --> 03:20.054
CHEOLMA GIRLS' MIDDLE SCHOOL BULLDOZER

39
03:20.138 --> 03:21.639
Okay, almost there.

40
03:25.143 --> 03:26.436
Defeat.

41
03:26.519 --> 03:27.478
Ah, sh…

42
03:33.985 --> 03:35.778
Oh, what should I eat?

43
03:42.869 --> 03:45.163
BYEON-HYEOK-JUN: IF YOU CAN'T REACH ME GO TO SPIDER STAFFING AGENCY

44
03:45.246 --> 03:46.706
"Spider Staffing Agency?"

45
03:52.628 --> 03:54.922
BYEON HYEOK-JUN

46
03:58.343 --> 04:01.220
The number you have dialed is currently unavailable.

47
04:01.304 --> 04:02.347
What the hell?

48
04:02.430 --> 04:03.806
…after the tone.

49
04:07.393 --> 04:08.895
Spider…

50
04:09.520 --> 04:10.813
SPIDER STAFFING AGENCY

51
04:10.897 --> 04:14.567
You could've left an address. It's not like there's only one Spider Staffing…

52
04:16.611 --> 04:18.071
I guess there is only one.

53
04:19.655 --> 04:23.368
SPIDER STAFFING AGENCY

54
04:28.790 --> 04:30.958
SPIDER STAFFING AGENCY

55
04:32.293 --> 04:33.920
Suspicious.

56
04:35.338 --> 04:37.423
Am I about to be caught in a web?

57
04:52.605 --> 04:53.940
Oh. Hello?

58
04:54.023 --> 04:55.483
- Welcome. - Thanks.

59
04:55.983 --> 04:57.527
Are you looking for a job?

60
04:58.861 --> 05:01.030
Oh, um… One sec.

61
05:01.531 --> 05:04.200
I'm looking for this guy here.

62
05:04.826 --> 05:06.786
Byeon Hyeok-jun. He's a little taller than me.

63
05:06.869 --> 05:08.746
Thirty years old. Looks a bit dumb.

64
05:08.830 --> 05:10.498
Do you know if he worked here?

65
05:12.583 --> 05:14.127
Oh, Hyeok-jun, yes?

66
05:14.210 --> 05:15.169
Uh-huh.

67
05:16.462 --> 05:17.296
Older sis?

68
05:20.675 --> 05:22.093
- Younger sister. - Ah.

69
05:24.178 --> 05:26.556
Mr. Hyeok-jun told you about us?

70
05:27.056 --> 05:28.224
Oh, um…

71
05:28.307 --> 05:31.310
Here. He sent this to me, and now he won't pick up.

72
05:31.394 --> 05:33.354
Go ahead. You can read it.

73
05:34.313 --> 05:37.275
It says, "If you can't reach me, go to Spider Staffing Agency."

74
05:38.818 --> 05:41.863
You know, we don't take tally on each of the employees.

75
05:41.946 --> 05:45.700
But he worked as your temp, right? So, where was he sent to work?

76
05:47.952 --> 05:50.371
Sorry, but we can't disclose that information.

77
05:51.539 --> 05:54.625
We're obligated to protect the information of our workers and the client.

78
05:54.709 --> 05:56.419
Protect their information?

79
05:58.546 --> 06:00.798
You hear how strange that sounds, right?

80
06:01.340 --> 06:02.842
Did you call the authorities?

81
06:03.342 --> 06:04.343
Huh?

82
06:04.427 --> 06:07.305
You should report a family member missing if you can't find them.

83
06:07.889 --> 06:11.642
But perhaps that's not what Hyeok-jun thought was the right course of action,

84
06:11.726 --> 06:14.187
since he told you to come here instead.

85
06:14.729 --> 06:17.857
Hold up now. How is it that you know who I am?

86
06:17.940 --> 06:19.442
What exactly did he say to you?

87
06:28.409 --> 06:30.786
The silent treatment. This boomer.

88
06:33.331 --> 06:34.790
I can take this, right?

89
06:34.874 --> 06:37.877
You better answer the phone when the cops start calling.

90
06:39.003 --> 06:40.838
Give me a ring when you need a job.

91
06:41.881 --> 06:44.258
I think you might do a better job than your little brother.

92
06:44.342 --> 06:46.302
I'm his younger sister!

93
06:58.981 --> 07:01.776
I'm afraid this isn't enough to file a missing person's report.

94
07:02.276 --> 07:05.154
For most of these cases, it's a runaway or a prank.

95
07:46.696 --> 07:47.863
Excuse me.

96
07:49.156 --> 07:52.410
Why are you following me? I've seen you for blocks now.

97
07:53.452 --> 07:54.954
Mmm.

98
07:56.706 --> 07:58.499
Observant one, aren't you?

99
07:59.500 --> 08:01.335
Your brother never noticed.

100
08:05.339 --> 08:06.799
You know my brother?

101
08:06.882 --> 08:09.594
I do. Byeon Hyeok-jun.

102
08:14.807 --> 08:18.060
What is with this day? God…

103
08:19.228 --> 08:21.147
I think there's something I can help you with.

104
08:21.647 --> 08:23.691
Why don't we have a little chat?

105
08:25.735 --> 08:27.236
WORKERS' COMPENSATION UNION EUM YEON-JOO

106
08:27.320 --> 08:28.904
"Accident investigator?"

107
08:37.288 --> 08:39.123
Are you saying Byeon Hyeok-jun…

108
08:39.665 --> 08:41.626
What are you saying, exactly?

109
08:42.251 --> 08:43.586
We'll get to that.

110
08:44.837 --> 08:49.258
You should know there's a white-robed ghost standing behind you, spying on us.

111
08:56.015 --> 08:57.558
Are you blind? It's just an apron.

112
08:58.267 --> 09:01.354
Then, what about the baby at the window who's staring?

113
09:10.571 --> 09:14.408
The two of you are so different. You aren't worried?

114
09:14.492 --> 09:16.035
Of course I'm worried.

115
09:17.036 --> 09:18.454
I'm terrified every day.

116
09:19.413 --> 09:22.708
When my budget is so tight that I can't pay rent until it's beyond late.

117
09:22.792 --> 09:24.877
Or when my last pair of leggings runs.

118
09:24.960 --> 09:26.879
Or when a friend invites me to their wedding.

119
09:26.962 --> 09:30.508
Hospital bills, or taxi fare, or not being able to share my Netflix password,

120
09:30.591 --> 09:32.134
it all makes me worried.

121
09:33.636 --> 09:36.681
So, when it comes to ghosts or whatever,

122
09:38.516 --> 09:39.767
they don't even make the list.

123
09:39.850 --> 09:41.644
Now tell me where my brother is.

124
09:43.145 --> 09:44.814
You want my best guess,

125
09:45.314 --> 09:48.484
Hyeok-jun is at the threshold of the other world.

126
09:52.446 --> 09:53.698
Yeah, I'm confused now.

127
09:53.781 --> 09:55.282
I got a C in poetry,

128
09:55.783 --> 10:00.121
so as fun as this game is, just give me his address and I'll find him myself.

129
10:00.204 --> 10:02.456
That was not poetry. I meant it.

130
10:02.957 --> 10:04.041
Literally.

131
10:08.045 --> 10:09.463
All right, enough.

132
10:09.964 --> 10:12.508
Are you saying Byeon Hyeok-jun can be found, or maybe not?

133
10:12.591 --> 10:13.884
I think so.

134
10:14.385 --> 10:16.804
If we play this smart.

135
10:16.887 --> 10:18.639
His workplace is connected to the other world,

136
10:18.723 --> 10:20.516
so we have to go there and find him.

137
10:22.101 --> 10:26.313
What the hell am I doing here listening to this nonsense? Seriously.

138
10:27.106 --> 10:30.025
How about you go to his workplace and enjoy the threshold?

139
10:31.736 --> 10:33.696
You're not gonna look for your brother?

140
10:37.158 --> 10:39.410
You may not want to believe me, but…

141
10:41.454 --> 10:43.664
if you wanna find him, I'm you're best bet.

142
10:45.040 --> 10:46.751
Now, are you ready to listen?

143
10:49.295 --> 10:54.800
BYEON HYEOK-JUN: IF YOU CAN'T REACH ME, GO TO SPIDER STAFFING AGEN CY

144
11:00.431 --> 11:01.432
Hey, listen.

145
11:02.057 --> 11:03.601
Imagine there's this gig.

146
11:04.101 --> 11:06.270
It may pay way over minimum wage.

147
11:06.353 --> 11:08.272
Maybe many, many times more.

148
11:09.523 --> 11:10.983
But the price is…

149
11:13.611 --> 11:15.863
all this messed-up stuff keeps coming,

150
11:15.946 --> 11:19.408
and I mean it's like these monsters, bugs, and spirits that trap you--

151
11:19.492 --> 11:21.994
I'd do it. I'd beg to.

152
11:22.578 --> 11:25.748
How would you be able to work with creatures, or whatever they are?

153
11:25.831 --> 11:28.959
You're scared of bugs? I'm scared of being poor.

154
11:35.090 --> 11:40.638
SPIDER STAFFING AGENCY

155
11:51.857 --> 11:53.859
Hello. Spider Staffing Agency.

156
11:56.237 --> 11:57.613
How can I help you?

157
11:58.197 --> 11:59.824
I want a temp job, okay?

158
12:06.664 --> 12:09.375
NEW WORLD CINEMA, PART-TIME JOB 50 TIMES THE DAILY WAGE, 11 P.M. - 5 A.M.

159
12:09.458 --> 12:11.627
WHY AREN'T YOU ANSWERING? GOING TO SPIDER STAFFING AGENCY

160
12:11.710 --> 12:13.337
REPORTED YOU MISSING MET EUM YEON-JOO

161
12:13.420 --> 12:16.090
Seriously, Byeon Hyeok-jun, you're such a pain in the ass.

162
12:16.173 --> 12:17.591
AT A WEIRD PART-TIME JOB TO FIND YOU

163
12:22.388 --> 12:23.347
Huh.

164
12:24.473 --> 12:26.934
Looks like this place is crawling with people.

165
12:32.898 --> 12:34.984
First, if you want to find your brother,

166
12:35.067 --> 12:37.695
you need to find a passage to the other world.

167
12:38.529 --> 12:41.699
To do that, you must pretend you're working a temp job.

168
12:41.782 --> 12:44.118
If they find out you have an ulterior motive,

169
12:44.201 --> 12:45.578
it could get dangerous.

170
12:51.959 --> 12:54.712
Oh, hey. You must be the temp.

171
12:54.795 --> 12:56.547
Oh, yes, hello.

172
12:57.089 --> 12:58.465
You have pretty eyes.

173
13:00.509 --> 13:02.344
- I'm Byeon Ji-yoon. - Mm.

174
13:02.845 --> 13:04.763
- You from Spider? - First placement.

175
13:07.266 --> 13:09.226
A Spider girl, huh?

176
13:11.812 --> 13:13.439
Hm. Tell me something.

177
13:13.522 --> 13:15.691
Have you ever worked at a theater before?

178
13:17.151 --> 13:19.570
A bit. One summer during my school break.

179
13:19.653 --> 13:22.156
- Oh, three months learning everything. - Yes.

180
13:22.239 --> 13:23.282
Mm.

181
13:24.617 --> 13:26.869
Oh. That's nice.

182
13:33.042 --> 13:34.543
Do you ever smoke?

183
13:34.627 --> 13:37.087
- Uh-huh. - That's nice.

184
13:37.588 --> 13:41.592
Second, there will be a hindrance guarding the passage.

185
13:42.676 --> 13:45.930
I don't know what form they'll take, but…

186
13:48.349 --> 13:51.518
you'll have the feeling that maybe you shouldn't be alone together.

187
13:53.312 --> 13:54.772
If you find them…

188
13:59.026 --> 14:00.152
tase them.

189
14:00.235 --> 14:01.528
Before they strike.

190
14:08.118 --> 14:09.662
- Ah. - I can't remember…

191
14:09.745 --> 14:11.956
Hello. Welcome to New World Cinema.

192
14:12.039 --> 14:14.750
- It's freaky with no one here. - Let's get to work.

193
14:23.175 --> 14:24.843
Here. Enjoy the movie.

194
14:38.065 --> 14:40.609
Third, you won't see anything right now,

195
14:40.693 --> 14:42.945
but when you get to the job, in the dark,

196
14:43.570 --> 14:46.031
you'll be able to locate all of the missing text.

197
14:50.119 --> 14:52.121
Look for the name of the place where you're working.

198
14:52.204 --> 14:54.248
INTERNET CAFÉ, POWER OUTLET, COVENIENCE STORE, FRIDGE…

199
14:54.331 --> 14:57.418
Once you find that, the door to the other world is right next to it.

200
14:57.501 --> 14:58.711
PUB, FRYER, MILK DELIVERY, 505…

201
14:58.794 --> 15:00.796
Take care of the hindrance, go through the passage,

202
15:00.879 --> 15:02.339
you'll be able to meet your brother.

203
15:02.423 --> 15:03.340
MOVIE THEATER, SCREEN 7

204
15:05.759 --> 15:07.636
"Screen 7?"

205
15:37.332 --> 15:40.085
A total of eight people have entered Screen 6.

206
15:40.961 --> 15:43.547
What? But we only sold seven tickets.

207
15:44.798 --> 15:45.632
What?

208
15:45.716 --> 15:48.135
I have eight checked tickets here.

209
15:49.136 --> 15:50.137
That's weird.

210
15:50.220 --> 15:51.638
We definitely sold seven tickets.

211
15:52.139 --> 15:54.141
Are you telling me that this other person is

212
15:54.641 --> 15:55.559
a ghost?

213
15:57.186 --> 15:59.354
Hey, I'm, just kidding. Did I scare you?

214
15:59.438 --> 16:01.440
Go help the audience out of Screen 5 and clean up.

215
16:01.523 --> 16:02.357
Yeah.

216
16:04.568 --> 16:06.779
This guy with the shitty jokes.

217
16:10.616 --> 16:12.993
God, did they keep missing their mouths?

218
16:26.590 --> 16:30.010
Excuse me, sir. There's no post-credits scene in this one, okay?

219
16:32.137 --> 16:34.431
I said there's no post-credits scene.

220
16:48.695 --> 16:52.699
Oh, shit. What the hell? Are these kids playing with slime?

221
16:55.577 --> 16:56.495
Oh.

222
16:58.080 --> 17:00.124
LOOKING FOR SOMEONE TO SHARE A HOT, SIZZLING TIME

223
17:00.207 --> 17:02.459
Damn it. A hot night, my ass.

224
17:06.088 --> 17:07.297
What the hell?

225
17:12.136 --> 17:13.929
Can I help you, sir?

226
17:20.185 --> 17:21.937
Are you a flasher or something?

227
17:25.983 --> 17:28.068
Get out of here! Go! Sick freak!

228
17:39.496 --> 17:41.957
What the hell? How did he do that?

229
17:44.001 --> 17:46.253
There are all kinds of perverts out there.

230
17:52.259 --> 17:53.802
- Ji-yoon. - Ah!

231
17:54.386 --> 17:55.512
What's that?

232
17:56.430 --> 18:00.058
It's a perv's coat. Must be a kink or something, so he might come back for it.

233
18:00.142 --> 18:03.312
Oh, it's probably the flasher. Hm.

234
18:03.395 --> 18:05.439
But it's also hard to confirm since

235
18:06.106 --> 18:07.107
nobody saw him.

236
18:09.359 --> 18:11.612
I know a flasher when I see a flasher.

237
18:12.112 --> 18:14.031
That man has done this before.

238
18:14.114 --> 18:16.575
The other temps, they're not so sure.

239
18:16.658 --> 18:18.327
They say he's a ghost.

240
18:19.953 --> 18:24.041
- Oh, for real? You can't buy that. - You've got guts, right?

241
18:25.709 --> 18:26.835
Check.

242
18:28.045 --> 18:29.338
Keep up the good work.

243
18:46.063 --> 18:47.481
Life's not fair.

244
18:47.564 --> 18:50.400
What kind of a ghost has more clothes than I do?

245
19:00.077 --> 19:03.580
LOST AND FOUND

246
19:09.878 --> 19:11.797
Ah, jeez. Come on.

247
19:11.880 --> 19:12.923
Knock, knock.

248
19:13.423 --> 19:15.092
Excuse me.

249
19:16.051 --> 19:17.886
Oh, yes. Can I help you?

250
19:19.054 --> 19:22.641
I, um, was in screen number six.

251
19:23.517 --> 19:27.479
CinemaScope shouldn't be projected in a movie theater made for VistaVision.

252
19:28.105 --> 19:31.608
You should at least mask the letterbox, but you didn't even do that.

253
19:32.484 --> 19:35.195
- Huh? - The screen is blurry on the edges.

254
19:36.905 --> 19:38.448
It ruins the immersion.

255
19:39.408 --> 19:41.159
Ah.

256
19:41.994 --> 19:45.622
Ah, sorry. I don't watch movies enough to know that.

257
19:49.042 --> 19:50.794
You really don't watch movies?

258
19:50.877 --> 19:51.753
Yeah.

259
19:56.842 --> 19:58.635
Hey, are you all right?

260
20:02.973 --> 20:05.183
True or false, Bong Joon Ho, the director of Parasite,

261
20:05.267 --> 20:07.602
which won Best Picture, Director, International Feature,

262
20:07.686 --> 20:10.564
and Original Screenplay at the 92nd Academy Awards,

263
20:10.647 --> 20:12.065
is the father of Bong Tae-gyu,

264
20:12.149 --> 20:14.526
an actor known for his role in the movie Family Ties?

265
20:14.609 --> 20:16.153
- Huh?

266
20:16.236 --> 20:17.279
Which is it?

267
20:19.531 --> 20:21.074
- True? - I'm afraid it's false.

268
20:21.158 --> 20:22.659
True or false?

269
20:22.743 --> 20:25.287
Lee Dong-jin, a film critic with the best recognition in Korea

270
20:25.370 --> 20:27.831
and known as the idol of the film critic world,

271
20:27.914 --> 20:29.458
wears red glasses. Which is it?

272
20:29.541 --> 20:30.500
It's false.

273
20:30.584 --> 20:31.585
Nope. True.

274
20:31.668 --> 20:34.421
Shit. Who the hell wears red glasses?

275
20:34.504 --> 20:36.256
You're terrible at movie trivia.

276
20:37.674 --> 20:40.302
One more chance. What's this movie?

277
20:45.390 --> 20:47.893
Umbrella. Rain. Rain.

278
20:49.478 --> 20:50.896
Smile? Is it smile?

279
20:51.813 --> 20:52.814
One more time.

280
20:55.484 --> 20:58.195
Huh. You run over…

281
20:59.863 --> 21:02.824
Umbrella. Rain. Smile?

282
21:02.908 --> 21:03.867
It's raining.

283
21:03.950 --> 21:06.828
You use an umbrella and smile.

284
21:06.912 --> 21:08.205
Is it…

285
21:13.627 --> 21:14.544
Uh…

286
21:15.420 --> 21:18.298
Temptation… of Wolves?

287
21:23.387 --> 21:24.388
Well,

288
21:25.514 --> 21:26.765
you beat me.

289
21:26.848 --> 21:28.225
Guess you do watch movies.

290
21:28.308 --> 21:29.935
Oh, I got it right? Man.

291
21:31.603 --> 21:33.021
Was he a lunatic or something?

292
21:33.105 --> 21:34.689
Ji-yoon?

293
21:35.232 --> 21:36.775
Who were you talking to just now?

294
21:37.275 --> 21:40.445
Some crazy guy just quizzed me out of nowhere. What's his deal?

295
21:40.529 --> 21:43.323
The movie quiz guy? That bastard came again?

296
21:43.407 --> 21:44.408
Did anything happen?

297
21:44.491 --> 21:45.909
He just left.

298
21:46.410 --> 21:47.953
Oh, then you were lucky.

299
21:48.453 --> 21:50.580
I heard that if you get three questions wrong in a row,

300
21:50.664 --> 21:52.707
he stabs you in the mouth with a pick.

301
21:52.791 --> 21:54.376
Or was it he rips your mouth open?

302
21:54.876 --> 21:58.588
He definitely stabs you with something. You must have done well.

303
22:01.591 --> 22:04.052
Ji-yoon? What about Screen 7? Is everyone in?

304
22:04.719 --> 22:07.597
Oh, there's no one in Screen 7. You don't have to play the movie.

305
22:08.098 --> 22:10.100
Huh? There's someone inside.

306
22:10.183 --> 22:12.436
Oh, come on, quit joking.

307
22:12.936 --> 22:16.314
I'm not. The projectionist said there's one person in Screen 7.

308
22:18.483 --> 22:19.359
What?

309
22:20.110 --> 22:22.362
Shit, maybe someone went into the wrong theater.

310
22:22.446 --> 22:23.530
Go check it out.

311
22:30.912 --> 22:32.038
Okay.

312
22:36.001 --> 22:38.628
Look for the name of the place where you're working.

313
22:39.421 --> 22:42.132
Once you find that, the door to the other world is right next to it.

314
22:42.215 --> 22:43.300
MOVIE THEATER, SCREEN 7

315
22:43.383 --> 22:45.719
If you take care of the hindrance and go through the passage,

316
22:45.802 --> 22:47.262
you'll be able to meet your brother.

317
23:19.503 --> 23:20.545
Excuse me.

318
23:32.224 --> 23:33.517
The hindrance.

319
23:46.029 --> 23:46.988
Excuse me.

320
23:48.573 --> 23:50.492
Can I take your ticket, please?

321
24:05.006 --> 24:06.841
In lane eight, we have Byeon Ji-yoon

322
24:06.925 --> 24:08.552
from Cheolma Girls' Middle School.

323
24:08.635 --> 24:10.470
She is the favorite to win coming into the race.

324
24:10.554 --> 24:12.305
Oh my God. What the…

325
24:13.974 --> 24:15.433
Is anyone in the projection room?

326
24:16.518 --> 24:19.396
What is this? What's going on? How did you get this?

327
24:22.732 --> 24:25.527
That sound of the pistol means we're off!

328
24:31.408 --> 24:33.159
Open up! Open up!

329
24:33.243 --> 24:34.786
Hey! Open this door!

330
24:49.509 --> 24:52.512
Open the door! Please! Please! Come on, open up!

331
25:05.108 --> 25:07.360
What? What is this? How did I…

332
25:19.289 --> 25:21.875
This isn't happening. Come on.

333
25:26.838 --> 25:27.672
Screw it.

334
25:44.481 --> 25:45.857
Wake up! Damn it!

335
25:46.524 --> 25:47.651
How do I wake up?

336
25:49.319 --> 25:51.655
Stay back! Stay back, please!

337
26:11.966 --> 26:15.679
Byeon Ji-yoon! Byeon Ji-yoon!

338
26:15.762 --> 26:20.600
Byeon Ji-yoon! Byeon Ji-yoon! Byeon Ji-yoon!

339
26:21.267 --> 26:25.105
Byeon Ji-yoon! Byeon Ji-yoon!

340
26:25.188 --> 26:28.983
Byeon Ji-yoon! Byeon Ji-yoon!

341
26:29.067 --> 26:30.110
Who the hell's doing this?

342
26:30.860 --> 26:32.862
- Byeon Ji-yoon! - Is anyone here?

343
26:32.946 --> 26:35.907
Byeon Ji-yoon! Byeon Ji-yoon!

344
26:35.990 --> 26:39.285
Byeon Ji-yoon! Byeon Ji-yoon!

345
26:48.586 --> 26:49.587
Oh!

346
26:51.673 --> 26:52.632
Ji-yoon.

347
26:57.053 --> 26:58.763
What are you doing with that chair?

348
27:00.557 --> 27:01.641
Are you working out?

349
27:05.019 --> 27:06.688
Ah, no, I just…

350
27:07.689 --> 27:11.317
The projector was playing something weird, so I thought I would look.

351
27:12.986 --> 27:16.614
The projector isn't your purview, so you should go back down.

352
27:16.698 --> 27:20.869
Oh, come on! It's playing something now for an empty room.

353
27:20.952 --> 27:22.162
You know,

354
27:23.037 --> 27:26.124
this machine can act weird sometimes.

355
27:28.877 --> 27:30.086
- Ji-yoon. - God!

356
27:30.170 --> 27:31.129
Get a grip.

357
27:32.839 --> 27:36.259
Only thing you need is time to make it through the night.

358
27:36.926 --> 27:37.802
Okay?

359
27:39.763 --> 27:40.805
So…

360
27:43.808 --> 27:44.809
how about a smoke?

361
27:44.893 --> 27:45.894
Ugh.

362
27:45.977 --> 27:47.979
- Oh, yeah. - Fuck off, seriously!

363
27:59.866 --> 28:00.992
What the hell?

364
28:06.915 --> 28:07.999
Oh my God.

365
28:11.336 --> 28:12.420
It's not…

366
28:13.254 --> 28:14.672
It's not… I can explain.

367
28:14.756 --> 28:15.673
Don't--

368
28:16.299 --> 28:17.258
Get away!

369
28:20.178 --> 28:22.222
- It's you, wasn't it? - What do you mean, me?

370
28:22.305 --> 28:24.057
You're the hindrance!

371
28:24.140 --> 28:25.433
It's not me, I swear!

372
28:54.420 --> 28:55.255
Hello?

373
28:56.172 --> 28:57.423
Ms. Byeon Ji-yoon?

374
28:58.508 --> 28:59.717
You're Spider?

375
28:59.801 --> 29:02.303
Yes, Spider Staffing Agency. Why are you answering?

376
29:02.387 --> 29:03.972
- Where's the manager? - Uh…

377
29:04.722 --> 29:08.852
Well, I, uh, tackled the crazy manager. Guy was a bastard.

378
29:08.935 --> 29:10.728
Gave me the creeps from the start.

379
29:10.812 --> 29:13.398
What do you mean "tackled him?" Why would you do that?

380
29:14.023 --> 29:15.900
- Uh… - Where is he now?

381
29:17.110 --> 29:18.695
Is he okay? Where's the manager?

382
29:22.323 --> 29:23.700
Put him on the phone.

383
29:25.076 --> 29:27.996
Ms. Byeon Ji-yoon, what the hell are you doing over there?

384
29:29.038 --> 29:31.291
Why would you do something we didn't ask of you?

385
29:31.374 --> 29:34.752
We sent you there to do one job. I can't have you doing something else.

386
29:36.462 --> 29:37.505
Screen…

387
29:38.464 --> 29:39.382
Hindrance…

388
29:49.809 --> 29:50.685
INSECTICIDE

389
29:50.768 --> 29:51.978
At least there's this.

390
30:14.709 --> 30:16.085
Come at me, bastard.

391
30:18.838 --> 30:23.009
Hey! Asshole? It's you, isn't it? Are you listening? Do you know who I am?

392
30:23.092 --> 30:25.136
I ran for Cheolma Girls' School.

393
30:49.786 --> 30:51.245
Agh, shit!

394
30:56.834 --> 30:58.127
I'm gonna kill you.

395
31:02.632 --> 31:04.384
You scumbag!

396
31:49.095 --> 31:50.972
Who says I can't finish strong?

397
31:51.639 --> 31:53.766
I fucking persist, damn it.

398
32:02.483 --> 32:05.653
After you eliminate the hindrance, find the door.

399
32:08.740 --> 32:11.451
Movie theater, Screen 7.

400
32:20.460 --> 32:22.420
What door was she talking about?

401
32:26.382 --> 32:27.717
A door handle?

402
32:54.035 --> 32:55.078
Byeon Hyeok-jun?

403
33:01.292 --> 33:02.126
Oh.

404
33:02.210 --> 33:03.336
Oh. Oh!

405
33:11.302 --> 33:13.096
Oh, oh-oh! What is this?!

406
33:18.935 --> 33:20.853
Wait, hold on.

407
33:21.395 --> 33:22.271
Hold on.

408
33:22.355 --> 33:25.066
MISSED CALL BYEON JI-YOON

409
33:25.149 --> 33:26.150
BYEON JI-YOON WHERE ARE YOU?

410
33:31.864 --> 33:32.824
Wait, what…

411
33:33.324 --> 33:34.242
Hold on.

412
33:36.577 --> 33:39.413
Wh… What's this? No, Ji-yoon! What did you do?

413
33:39.497 --> 33:41.207
AT A WEIRD PART-TIME JOB TO FIND YOU

414
33:41.290 --> 33:42.667
Tell me you didn't do this!
